# AI Railway Track Crack Detection

**Detect • Locate • Alert** – Byte Race 2026 (Idea Submission)
Vivekananda College of Engineering & Technology (VCET), Puttur

## Problem
Railway tracks are mostly inspected by hand, with workers walking long stretches. This is slow, risky, and easy to get wrong, especially at night or in bad weather. Small cracks can go unnoticed until they grow, causing derailments and costly emergency repairs.

## Solution
A low-cost, rail-riding robot with a Raspberry Pi camera that uses AI to detect track cracks, tags their GPS location, and alerts maintenance teams through a live dashboard.

## Key Features
1. **AI Crack Detection** – a lightweight model on the Raspberry Pi spots cracks in live camera footage with a confidence score.
2. **GPS Defect Mapping** – each crack is logged with location, time, and image.
3. **Smart Alerts** – severity-based alerts (minor / moderate / critical) via Telegram/SMS, plus a dashboard for maintenance planning.

## System Architecture
Data Capture → AI Detection → Locate (GPS) → Database → Dashboard & Alerts

